report.summary:
I wrote docs/reading-the-code.md, a guide to reading the code. It is 828 lines, in 22 steps plus a step that puts the pieces together. The steps follow the four areas and the import order:
- signature: step 1 (signing, keygen);
- node: steps 2 to 16 (the consensus types; the ledger from amounts and names up to ApplyBlock and ProposeBlock; the driver; then the node's event loop, intake and pools, one height, double-sign proofs and certificates, the snapshot and sign log, catch-up, and writing the record);
- API/CDN: steps 17 to 19 (the HTTP routes, relay and peers, the commands);
- UI: steps 20 to 22 (key file and pin, the wallet's actions, the pages).

Each step gives:
- what it is for, with a link to the area doc that explains why;
- its files, in reading order;
- a table from each concept to the type or function that holds it;
- the facts later steps take as given;
- a Go idiom note where an idiom first appears;
- the tests to read and one go test command.

The last step traces three journeys hop by hop, naming each function: a payment from the wallet's signature to the wallet's verified state, then a freeze, then a ⅔ name action. A closing table maps each of the 54 production files and the 3 templates to its step.

Every command was run on a copy of the tree that held only the packages up to its step, and each passed.
- The test counts match the guide: 16, 17, 16, 3, 4, 13 and 123 for consensus and ledger; 18 for the driver; 3, 24, 21, 18, 24, 14, 12, 13 and 9 for node; 16, 35 and 11 for ui; 12 for the commands.
- The node commands cover all 138 node tests except the 9 chaos tests, and each test falls in exactly one step. The 9 chaos tests run in the last step's full suite.
- go test -race ./... and go test -C ui -race ./... pass, and the demo started (make build, then bin/demo briefly) in scratch.

A script found that every name the guide cites exists in the code. All relative links and anchors resolve.

I replaced README.md's Layout section, which still said Ed25519, with a package map by area that points to the guide. docs/README.md lists the guide under General. No Go file or template changed. The code notes are below; the first one is a real bug.

codeNotes.note:
'Snapshot' names four things:
- each pool's copy of its pending entries;
- Node.snapshot, the committed view for checkpoints;
- the Snapshot type a read route returns;
- the snapshot file (savedSnapshot, Config.SnapshotPath).
